Vercel Speed Insights Installation Complete
==========================================

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the ANM project.

## What was implemented:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in package.json

### 2. Component Integration
- Added SpeedInsights component import to src/App.tsx
- Integrated the `<SpeedInsights />` component into the main App component
- Placed the component outside the Routes wrapper to ensure it renders on all pages

### 3. Implementation Details
- **Framework**: React 18.3.1 with Vite 5.1.4
- **Package Manager**: npm (package-lock.json updated)
- **Integration Path**: `@vercel/speed-insights/react` (React-specific import)
- **Location**: Main App component (src/App.tsx)

### Files Modified:
1. `package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights to dependencies
2. `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and its dependencies
3. `src/App.tsx` - Added import and component integration

### Implementation Approach:
Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart):
- Imported SpeedInsights from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'
- Added the component at the root level of the App component
- Used React Fragment (<></>) to wrap Routes and SpeedInsights together
- Maintained proper indentation and code structure

### Verification Completed:
✅ Build successful (npm run build)
✅ Linter passed with no errors (npm run lint)
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ No breaking changes introduced

### Next Steps for Deployment:
Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start tracking performance metrics
2. Verify the script is loaded by checking for `/<unique-path>/script.js` in the page head
3. Performance data will appear in the Vercel Speed Insights dashboard after users visit the site

### Notes:
- The SpeedInsights component is a lightweight wrapper that loads the tracking script
- It will only be active when deployed on Vercel
- No additional configuration is required for basic functionality
- For advanced configuration options, refer to the Vercel Speed Insights documentation
